

-- Encapsulate action as objects allowing parameterization and decoupling of requests


-- Example -> order a food

-- Command pattern allows you to encapsulate actions as objects, decoupling the client from the receiver.

-- The command pattern is in which an object is used to encapsulate all the information needed to perform
an action or trigger an event at a later time.This information includes the method name , the object that owns the
method and the parameters for the method.

-- Controlling a light control

-- receiver -> command interface --> concrete classes --> Invoker class -> client class

-- When to use

  It is perfect for implementing features --> like scheduling, logging, undo, and redo.
  When you need to encapsulate operations as objects and control behaviour through the arrangement
  of these operations, the command pattern is very useful.

  Summary:
  It encapsulates the requests as objects, allowing the system to support complex command
  request, and operation management. It offers a flexible way to extend system funcitonality while maintaining decouling
  between the invoker and receiver.
